Q('l04', mk.long({ marks: 10, stem: r`An imagined taxi company buys a car for ₹6,25,000. Its value falls by $20\%$ of its value at the start of every year. Show all working.
(a) Show that the values of the car at the start of years $1, 2, 3, \ldots$ form a geometric progression, and find its value after $3$ years.
(b) After how many complete years does its value first fall below ₹2,50,000?
(c) The yearly falls in value also form a geometric progression. Write its first term and common ratio, and use the sum formula to find the total fall in value over the first $4$ years.`, model: J([`**(a)** Each year the value is multiplied by ${wl04.md[0]}, the same number every year, so the values form a geometric progression with $a = 625000$ and $r = 0.8$.`, `Value after $3$ years: ${wl04.md[1]}, that is ₹3,20,000.`, `**(b)** After $4$ years: ${wl04.md[2]}; after $5$ years: ${wl04.md[3]}.`, `Since ${wl04.md[4]} and ${wl04.md[5]}, the value first falls below ₹2,50,000 after $5$ years.`, `**(c)** The falls are $125000, 100000, 80000, 64000, \\ldots$ rupees: first term ${wl04f.md[0]}, common ratio $0.8$.`, `Total fall over $4$ years: ${wl04f.md[1]}, that is ₹3,69,000.`, `Check: ${wl04.md[6]}.`]), sol: 'Part (a) shows the value is multiplied by the same factor each year; part (b) compares successive terms with the limit; part (c) sums the GP of yearly falls and checks against the drop in value.', scheme: [['(a) ratio 0.8 each year', 1], ['(a) ₹3,20,000', 2], ['(b) values after 4 and 5 years', 2], ['(b) 5 years', 1], ['(c) first fall 125000, ratio 0.8', 1], ['(c) S₄ formula', 2], ['(c) ₹3,69,000', 1]], d: 3, c: 'application', t: [3, 2], time: 720 }), (C) => { wl04.verify(C); wl04f.verify(C); C.assert(gl04.term(4).eq(320000) && gl04.firstTerm('<', 250000) - 1 === 5, 'value and years'); C.assert(ratioOf(falls04).eq(Rat.of('0.8')) && falls04[0].eq(125000) && gl04f.sum(4).eq(369000) && gl04.term(1).sub(gl04.term(5)).eq(369000), 'falls GP'); C.model([320000, 5, 125000, 369000]); });
const gl05p = gp(400, 2), gl05q = gp(6400, q(1, 2));
